MatchingModule/documentation/MatchingModule/GraphProtocols/Graph/maximumMatching()":{"title":"maximumMatching()","kind":"symbol","role":"symbol","abstract":[{"text":"A maximum-cardinality matching by Edmonds’ blossom algorithm: for each still-free vertex in","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"vertex order, a breadth-first alternating search (rows in ","type":"text"},{"code":"incidentEdges","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" order) that","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"contracts blossoms and augments along the first free vertex found, skipping the vertices of","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"earlier failed searches. The matching returned is","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"this procedure’s, a documented function of the vertex order and rows. Parallel edges: the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"copy met first. Vertices of a search that fails are skipped by later searches. O(n · m · log n).","type":"text"}],"type":"topic","url":"\/documentation\/matchingmodule\/graphprotocols\/graph\/maximummatching()","identifier":"doc:\/\/MatchingModule\/documentation\/MatchingModule\/GraphProtocols\/Graph\/maximumMatching()","fragments":[{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"maximumMatching","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"() -> ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Matching","preciseIdentifier":"s:14MatchingModule0A0V","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":"<","kind":"text"},{"text":"Self","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":", ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Int","preciseIdentifier":"s:Si","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":">","kind":"text"}]}}}